<header class="phead"><div class="wrap"><h1>Agents we’ve shipped.</h1><p>These are examples, not a catalogue. They show the shape of what an agent can own end to end, and where we draw the line between machine and person. What we build for you is designed around your processes, including the ones you have every reason to keep to yourself.</p></div></header><section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="crew"><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/sterling' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Sterling</h3></span><p class="role">Working capital</p><p>Reads receivables and payables from the ERP, narrates the cash position daily, and drafts collection sequences ranked by recovery odds.</p><ul><li>Daily cash position, written not charted</li><li>Collections ranked by recovery odds</li><li>Disputed invoices held back automatically</li><li>Promise-to-pay tracked to the date</li></ul><span class="go">How Sterling works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/clark' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Clark</h3></span><p class="role">Payables</p><p>Extracts vendor invoices from any format and posts the payable straight into SAP or NetSuite, with duplicate detection before anything is released.</p><ul><li>Any format: PDF, scan, portal or email body</li><li>Duplicate and near-duplicate detection</li><li>Three-way match with tolerance rules</li><li>Coding proposed from history, not guessed</li></ul><span class="go">How Clark works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/tally' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Tally</h3></span><p class="role">Reconciliation</p><p>Balances sub-ledgers to the GL line by line and hands back a clean exception list instead of a spreadsheet nobody wants to open.</p><ul><li>Runs continuously, not at month-end</li><li>Variance commentary drafted for review</li><li>Accrual proposals with support attached</li><li>Break aging, so nothing sits unexplained</li></ul><span class="go">How Tally works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/chandler' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Chandler</h3></span><p class="role">Procurement</p><p>Runs RFQ to PO with multi-vendor negotiation across email, SMS and voice, then holds suppliers to the pricing schedule they agreed to.</p><ul><li>Multi-vendor RFQ across channels</li><li>Contract terms extracted and monitored</li><li>Price variance flagged against schedule</li><li>Award recommendation with the math shown</li></ul><span class="go">How Chandler works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/swift' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Swift</h3></span><p class="role">Order management</p><p>Turns inbound customer purchase order PDFs into clean sales orders in minutes rather than days, flagging only what genuinely needs a decision.</p><ul><li>PO document to sales order in minutes</li><li>Pricing and terms validated on intake</li><li>Only true exceptions routed to a person</li><li>Acknowledgement sent the same hour</li></ul><span class="go">How Swift works →</span></a><a class="agent" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/agents/quill' ) ); ?>"><span class="nm"><i></i><h3>Quill</h3></span><p class="role">Quotes &amp; CRM</p><p>Reads every inbound enquiry, prices it against your rules, and drafts the quote in your CRM so a rep is editing rather than starting cold.</p><ul><li>Every enquiry read, none dropped</li><li>Priced against your own rule set</li><li>Drafted in the CRM, ready to edit</li><li>Follow-up scheduled and tracked</li></ul><span class="go">How Quill works →</span></a></div><div class="bespoke"><h3>Your agents are built around your organization.</h3><p>The way you price, route, approve and escalate is years of accumulated judgment, and it's a real advantage. It belongs to you and it stays with you, we're not asking you to hand over your playbook or fit yourself into someone else's template. We start from how your business already works, encode that logic into agents built for your environment, and leave you with an operation that runs faster with exactly the things that make you good at it still intact.</p></div><p class="note">Every agent stops at an approval gate until it has earned its way out of one. Nothing releases cash, commits spend or touches a customer without a person saying so.</p></div></section><section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><h2>The difference is execution.</h2><p class="intro">Plenty of tools will now summarize a report or draft an email about a problem. An agent goes and resolves it. Receivables makes the clearest illustration because every business runs it, both columns end in the same place, with a person releasing the money.</p><div class="worlds"><div class="world manual"><p class="tag">Receivables → cash · assisted</p><ul><li>Pull the aging report out of SAP by hand</li><li>Guess which accounts to chase first</li><li>Chase across scattered email threads</li><li>Reconcile remittances line by line</li><li>See the true cash position at month-end</li></ul></div><div class="world agentic"><p class="tag">Receivables → cash · agent-run</p><ul><li>Aging and payables read live from the ERP</li><li>Cash position narrated every morning</li><li>Collection sequences drafted, prioritized by risk</li><li>Remittance exceptions listed, not hunted</li><li class="human">Human approves and releases</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="wrap"><h2>Bring us one workflow.</h2><p>Thirty minutes, no deck. Pick the process that costs you most in people, errors or delay, and we'll pressure-test whether an agent is genuinely the right answer for it.</p><ul class="cta-list"><li>An honest read on whether that workflow is a good agent candidate</li><li>What the first deployment would involve, and roughly what it costs</li><li>An honest answer if the sequencing is wrong and you should fix something else first</li></ul><a class="btn btn-lg" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/contact' ) ); ?>">Book a discovery call</a></div></section>
